  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the hateful textual claim",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'white genocide' overlaid on the South African flag, as the meme's overall intent is to incite racial hatred by falsely attributing genocidal intent to the national symbol. The user is implicitly positioned as the one who must understand or accept this false narrative, even though the text does not contain explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me'. The projection is onto the textual material because the hateful message is the core semiotic element being communicated and internalized by the viewer.",
